---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ProductImage from '../components/ProductImage.astro';
import { getProduct } from '../data/products';
import Placeholder from '../components/Placeholder.astro';
import Print from '../components/Print.astro';
import Flower from '../components/Flower.astro';
import Marquee from '../components/Marquee.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import '../styles/story.css';

const phrases = ['GUBBI = SPARROW', 'NAMMA BENGALURU', 'CHIKKA GUYS, DODDA FEELINGS', 'OLD CRAFT. NEW MISCHIEF.', 'SWALPA ADJUST MAADI', 'ONE TEA BEKU'];

// The route so far, drawn like a metro line. "Prototypes" is the live stop.
const stops = [
  { name: 'Gubbi Art Club', line: 'A room in Bengaluru where people come to paint, crochet and make a beautiful little mess.' },
  { name: 'One joke too many', line: 'Somebody said “Silk Board is a state of mind” and nobody could stop laughing. Or leave.' },
  { name: 'Six guys on paper', line: 'Traffic, tokens, the eternal ETA. Drawn before anyone said “gombe”.' },
  { name: 'Channapatna', line: 'Three visits, a lot of chai, and learning what the wood wants to be. The makers fixed our drawings.' },
  { name: 'Collection 01', line: 'Six characters, hand-turned, boxed, and on this site.', here: true },
  { name: 'Collection 02', line: 'On the lathe. Same hands, new stories.', next: true },
];
---
<Layout title="Our story: a sparrow, a city, six wooden guys | The Gubbi" description="Gubbi means sparrow in Kannada. The story of a small bird, a loud city, an art club, and six hand-turned wooden characters who refuse to get a real job." type="article">
<section class="story-hero">
 <div class="wrap story-hero-inner">
  <div class="story-hero-copy">
   <h1>Chikka gombe.<br/><em>Dodda</em> ooru.</h1>
   <p class="story-hero-lede">Small doll, big city. Gubbi means sparrow in Kannada. This is the story of a small bird, a very loud city, and six wooden guys who refuse to get a real job.</p>
   <a class="text-link" href="#sparrow">Scroll, boss <Icon/></a>
  </div>
  <div class="story-fan" aria-label="Three of the characters, as taped prints">
   <Print tilt={-7} tape="left" class="story-fan-a"><ProductImage product={getProduct('traffic-kumar')!} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 60vw, 360px" eager/></Print>
   <Print tilt={4} tape="top" class="story-fan-b"><ProductImage product={getProduct('yaavdu-dice')!} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 60vw, 360px" eager/></Print>
   <Print tilt={-2} tape="right" class="story-fan-c"><ProductImage product={getProduct('i-got-it-bruh')!} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 60vw, 360px" eager/></Print>
   <span class="story-stamp" aria-hidden="true"><Flower/><span>Made<br/>in traffic</span></span>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<Marquee phrases={phrases}/>

<section class="story-sparrow" id="sparrow">
 <div class="wrap story-sparrow-inner">
  <div class="story-sparrow-copy">
   <h2>Gubbi means <em>sparrow.</em></h2>
   <p>Small. Loud. Everywhere. The bird that used to sit on every window ledge in this city, stealing rice from ajji’s kitchen and losing every argument with a crow.</p>
   <p>Then one day you notice you haven’t seen one in a while. Every family here has a sparrow story like that. We took the name so we’d have a small reminder sitting on the desk: notice the little things before they go.</p>
   <a class="light-link" href="/philosophy#nest">What we want to do about it <Icon/></a>
  </div>
  <div class="story-sparrow-photo">
   <Print tilt={3} tape="top" caption="Where the sparrows used to sit."><Placeholder name="window-ledge" portrait alt=""/></Print>
   <Flower/>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="story-route" aria-labelledby="route-title">
 <div class="wrap">
  <header class="story-route-head"><h2 id="route-title">How we got <em>here.</em></h2><p>The route so far, drawn like a metro map because that’s how we think in this city. Mind the gap.</p></header>
  <ol class="story-line">
   {stops.map(stop=><li class:list={[stop.here && 'is-here', stop.next && 'is-next']}><span class="story-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3>{stop.name}{stop.here && <small>You are here</small>}{stop.next && <small>Next stop</small>}</h3><p>{stop.line}</p></li>)}
  </ol>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="story-between" aria-labelledby="between-title">
 <div class="wrap">
  <div class="story-between-head">
   <h2 id="between-title">Not the skyline.<br/><em>The ride home.</em></h2>
   <p>Not the landmarks. The particular chaos that makes you say “only in Bengaluru” while stuck under a flyover named after nobody you know. The shared joke. The filter coffee at the wrong time. That’s what we want to make things about — small enough for a desk, specific enough to start a fight in the group chat.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="story-collage">
   <div class="story-collage-col">
    <Print tilt={-3} tape="top" caption="Same jam. Different day."><ProductImage product={getProduct('silk-board-forever')!} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 92vw, 420px"/></Print>
    <Print tilt={4} tape="top" caption="Ship it. Refactor later."><ProductImage product={getProduct('i-got-it-bruh')!} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 92vw, 420px"/></Print>
   </div>
   <div class="story-collage-col">
    <Print tilt={2} tape="right" caption="Wrong time. Correct coffee." class="print--portrait"><Placeholder name="filter-coffee" portrait/></Print>
    <Print tilt={-2} tape="top" caption="7:40am. Already late."><Placeholder name="bengaluru-morning"/></Print>
   </div>
   <div class="story-collage-col">
    <Print tilt={-1} tape="left" caption="The first six, before they were wooden."><Placeholder name="sketchbook"/></Print>
    <Print tilt={3} tape="left" caption="Where they end up living." class="print--portrait"><Placeholder name="desk-corner" portrait/></Print>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="story-quote" aria-label="A note on adjusting">
 <div class="wrap">
  <Flower/>
  <blockquote><p>“Swalpa adjust maadi” is not a compromise. It’s a love language.</p></blockquote>
  <p class="story-quote-note">Please adjust a little. It is how this city fits ten people into an auto, and how we plan to fit an entire mood into a palm-sized piece of wood.</p>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="story-craft" aria-labelledby="craft-title">
 <div class="wrap story-craft-inner">
  <div class="story-craft-photo">
   <Print tilt={-4} tape="top" caption="Spin before shipping."><ProductImage product={getProduct('token-maxxer')!} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 92vw, 420px"/></Print>
   <Print tilt={5} tape="left" class="story-craft-photo-b" caption="Colour goes on while the wood spins."><Placeholder name="lac-sticks"/></Print>
  </div>
  <div class="story-craft-copy">
   <h2>Keep the craft.<br/>Change the <em>conversation.</em></h2>
   <p>Every Gubbi comes out of Channapatna’s turned-wood tradition — lathe, lac, a leaf for polish, and hands that have been doing this for generations. The gombe on your ajji’s shelf came from there. Ours do too, with slightly more existential dread on the base.</p>
   <p>The makers fixed our drawings. Corners became curves, colours became whatever lac was willing to do, and the characters got better for it. Each piece still comes off the lathe one at a time, so no two are quite the same.</p>
   <a class="button" href="/philosophy">How a gombe is made <Icon/></a>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="story-ways wrap" aria-labelledby="ways-title">
 <h2 id="ways-title">One gubbi.<br/><em>Two ways in.</em></h2>
 <div class="story-ways-grid">
  <a class="story-way story-way--shop" href="/shop">
   <div class="story-way-copy"><span class="story-way-kicker">The shop</span><h3>Take a little guy home.</h3><p>Hand-turned collectibles with local stories and very distinct personalities. All of them unemployed.</p><span class="story-way-link">Meet everyone <Icon/></span></div>
   <Print tilt={6} tape="top" class="story-way-print"><ProductImage product={getProduct('bartha-idini')!} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 92vw, 420px"/></Print>
  </a>
  <a class="story-way story-way--club" href="https://gubbiartclub.com">
   <div class="story-way-copy"><span class="story-way-kicker">Gubbi Art Club</span><h3>Make a little thing yourself.</h3><p>Art and craft workshops in Bengaluru for curious hands. Same spirit, with more paint on your clothes.</p><span class="story-way-link">See the workshops <Icon/></span></div>
   <Print tilt={-5} tape="left" class="story-way-print"><img src="/images/art-club-table.webp" alt="A workshop table at Gubbi Art Club, mid-session" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></Print>
  </a>
 </div>
</section>
</Layout>
